From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 21 Jan 2026 19:12:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: server: add dedicated IO threads with per-queue
 schedulers

tapdisk is multi-queue and multi-thread but every request still go
to the same lists and are handled in the main thread of tapdisk.

Create one IO thread per queue, each with its own scheduler and event
loop. Move queue-related events (ring, chkrng, stoppolling, bufcache)
from the main scheduler to the per-queue IO thread schedulers.

Add a wake mechanism (eventfd) so IO threads can wake the main scheduler
when requests are ready. tapdisk_vbd_queue_request() gains a 'final'
parameter to signal the last request in a batch, triggering the wake.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
